= Protocol (computing) =

== Overview ==
A '''protocol''' in computing is a defined set of rules, message structures, state transitions, and conventions that allows communicating systems to coordinate.

Protocols specify how information is formatted, exchanged, interpreted, and sequenced. They may operate between processes on one machine or across networks.

A protocol is an agreement about interaction, not a particular software implementation. Multiple implementations can interoperate when they conform to the same protocol.

== Boundaries ==
* protocol ≠ implementation
* protocol ≠ API
* protocol ≠ data format alone

